  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts a man drinking from a bottle, with text that reads 'when you don't have to see your ex future mother-in-law anymore.' The scene uses the visual of intoxication to symbolize relief or escape from a difficult interpersonal situation. The intent is to humorously convey the emotional release associated with no longer having to interact with a specific family member. While the content is not explicitly abusive, cyberbullying, or hateful toward any protected group, it does contain potentially harmful implications by trivializing complex family dynamics and emotional distress. The meme normalizes the idea of using alcohol as a coping mechanism for interpersonal conflict, which can be harmful by suggesting that avoidance or intoxication is an acceptable or even desirable response to difficult social situations. The humor is derived from the juxtaposition of the image (drinking) with the text (relief from a future mother-in-law), implying that the situation is so unpleasant that one would need to drink to cope. This can be seen as a form of emotional shorthand that may not be appropriate for all audiences, especially those who have experienced similar situations or who may be struggling with coping mechanisms. The meme does not contain any direct attacks on individuals based on protected characteristics, but it does contain content that could be interpreted as dismissive of the emotional complexity of family relationships and the potential harm of using alcohol as a coping strategy.",
